        192.87460327148438,
        277.4940490722656
      ],
      "text": "TB in children",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 19.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        280.15087890625,
        527.41259765625,
        297.3879089355469
      ],
      "text": "(75–77) Around 25 000–32 000 children are estimated to develop MDR/RR-TB every year  . In 2018,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        296.14501953125,
        527.435546875,
        310.5880432128906
      ],
      "text": "3398 children (aged below 15 years) were started on second-line treatment for MDR/RR-TB. After",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        309.34503173828125,
        527.4403686523438,
        323.7880554199219
      ],
      "text": "increasing to 5586 in 2019, due to the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic, this number dropped back",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.986592292785645,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        322.5448913574219,
        527.435546875,
        336.9879150390625
      ],
      "text": "to 3234 in 2020, representing only 2.5% of the total number of persons with MDR/RR-TB initiated on",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        332.95098876953125,
        527.4173583984375,
        350.1880187988281
      ],
      "text": "(78) treatment and only 10.1%–12.9% of the estimated number of children with incident MDR/RR-TB  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.992197036743164,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        348.9449157714844,
        527.294677734375,
        363.387939453125
      ],
      "text": "Treatment outcomes reported in a systematic review and individual patient data meta-analysis",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        362.14501953125,
        527.4422607421875,
        376.5880432128906
      ],
      "text": "conducted for the 2018 WHO DR-TB treatment guidelines, showed an overall successful treatment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        375.3450012207031,
        527.4268188476562,
        389.78802490234375
      ],
      "text": "outcome of 78% in children treated for MDR-TB (75% of confirmed and 89% of clinically diagnosed",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        385.75091552734375,
        527.4823608398438,
        402.9879150390625
      ],
      "text": "(79) children)  . Appropriate treatment of children with MDR/RR-TB with a WHO recommended regimen",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.95792007446289,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        401.7449951171875,
        527.4931030273438,
        416.1880187988281
      ],
      "text": "is an important step in ensuring a successful treatment outcome, as well as preventing the acquisition",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.986291885375977,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        414.9449157714844,
        527.20703125,
        429.387939453125
      ],
      "text": "of further drug resistance. Other measures to prevent drug resistance or limit its spread include",
